{"id":"mahabharata-7-167","work":"mahabharata","part":7,"partName":"द्रोणपर्व","partNameEn":"Drona Parva","unit":167,"title":"सप्तषष्ट्यधिकशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 167 · The Narayana weapon appears","summary":{"en":"When the Narayana weapon appears, the wind blows and the sky roars, and the Pandava army is struck with fear. Yudhishthira bids all lay down their arms, and Arjuna says he will not do so, since he is bound by his vow not to refuse a challenge.","kn":"ನಾರಾಯಣಾಸ್ತ್ರ ಪ್ರಕಟವಾದಾಗ ಗಾಳಿ ಬೀಸಿ ಆಕಾಶ ಗರ್ಜಿಸುತ್ತದೆ; ಪಾಂಡವ ಸೈನ್ಯ ಭಯಪಡುತ್ತದೆ. ಯುಧಿಷ್ಠಿರ ಎಲ್ಲರೂ ಆಯುಧ ಕೆಳಗಿಡಲು ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಅರ್ಜುನ ಸವಾಲನ್ನು ನಿರಾಕರಿಸದ ತನ್ನ ವ್ರತದಿಂದ ಹಾಗೆ ಮಾಡುವುದಿಲ್ಲವೆನ್ನುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"नारायणास्त्र प्रकट होने पर वायु चलती है और आकाश गरजता है, पाण्डव सेना भयभीत होती है। युधिष्ठिर सबको शस्त्र रखने को कहते हैं, और अर्जुन कहते हैं कि वे ऐसा नहीं करेंगे क्योंकि चुनौती न ठुकराने का उनका व्रत है।","te":"నారాయణాస్త్రం ప్రత్యక్షమవగా గాలి వీచి ఆకాశం గర్జిస్తుంది; పాండవసేన భయపడుతుంది. అందరినీ ఆయుధాలు వదలమని యుధిష్ఠిరుడు చెబుతాడు; సవాలును తిరస్కరించని తన వ్రతం వల్ల తాను అలా చేయనని అర్జునుడు అంటాడు.","ta":"நாராயணாஸ்திரம் தோன்றியதும் காற்று வீசி வானம் முழங்க, பாண்டவப் படை அஞ்சுகிறது. எல்லோரும் ஆயுதம் துறக்கும்படி யுதிஷ்டிரர் கூற, சவாலை மறுக்காத தன் விரதத்தால் அவ்வாறு செய்யமாட்டேன் என்கிறான் அர்ஜுனன்.","ml":"നാരായണാസ്ത്രം പ്രത്യക്ഷപ്പെടുമ്പോൾ കാറ്റ് വീശുന്നു, ആകാശം ഗർജിക്കുന്നു; പാണ്ഡവ സേന ഭയത്താൽ നിറയുന്നു. ആയുധം താഴെവെക്കാൻ യുധിഷ്ഠിരൻ എല്ലാവരോടും കൽപ്പിക്കുന്നു; വെല്ലുവിളി നിരസിക്കരുതെന്ന വ്രതത്താൽ ബന്ധിതനായതിനാൽ അങ്ങനെ ചെയ്യില്ലെന്ന് അർജുനൻ പറയുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 7.167; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Sep 22 2026","sections":[{"title":"नारायणास्त्रमोक्षपर्व","titleEn":"Narayanastramoksha Parva (Release of the Narayana weapon)","verses":[{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"प्रादुर्भूते ततस्तस्मिन्नस्त्रे नारायणे तदा ।\nप्रावात्सपृषतो वायुरनभ्रे स्तनयित्नुमान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When the Narayana weapon appeared, a wind with raindrops blew and thunder rolled from a cloudless sky."}},{"n":2,"text":"चचाल पृथिवी चापि चुक्षुभे च महोदधिः ।\nप्रतिस्रोतः प्रवृत्ताश्च गन्तुं तत्र समुद्रगाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The earth shook, the great ocean heaved, and the rivers began to flow backward."}},{"n":3,"text":"शिखराणि व्यदीर्यन्त गिरीणां तत्र भारत ।\nअपसव्यं मृगाश्चैव पाण्डुपुत्रान्प्रचक्रिरे ॥","meaning":{"en":"The mountain peaks split apart there, O Bharata, and the beasts passed the sons of Pandu keeping them on their left."}},{"n":4,"text":"तमसा चावकीर्यन्त सूर्यश्च कलुषोऽभवत् ।\nसंपतन्ति च भूतानि क्रव्यादानि प्रहृष्टवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Darkness spread, the sun turned murky, and flesh-eating creatures swooped down as if in delight."}},{"n":5,"text":"देवदानवगन्धर्वास्त्रस्ता आसन्विशां पते ।\nकथं कथाभवत्तीव्रा दृष्ट्वा तद्व्याकुलं महत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Gods, danavas and gandharvas were terrified, O lord of men; a sharp murmur arose as they saw that great confusion."}},{"n":6,"text":"व्यथिताः सर्वराजानस्तदा ह्यासन्विचेतसः ।\nतद्दृष्ट्वा घोररूपं तु द्रौणेरस्त्रं भयावहम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"All the kings were distressed and bewildered at the sight of that fearful, dreadful weapon of Drona's son."}},{"text":"धृतराष्ट्र उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Dhritarashtra said:"}},{"n":7,"text":"निवर्तितेषु सैन्येषु द्रोणपुत्रेण संयुगे ।\nभृशं शोकाभितप्तेन पितुर्वधममृष्यता ॥","meaning":{"en":"When Drona's son, scorched by grief and unable to bear his father's killing, had turned his armies back in the battle,"}},{"n":8,"text":"कुरूनापततो दृष्ट्वा धृष्टद्युम्नस्य रक्षणे ।\nको मन्त्रः पाण्डवेष्वासीत्तन्ममाचक्ष्व संजय ॥","meaning":{"en":"and when he saw the Kurus advancing to protect Dhrishtadyumna, what counsel was there among the Pandavas? Tell me that, Sanjaya."}},{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":9,"text":"प्रागेव विद्रुतान्दृष्ट्वा धार्तराष्ट्रान्युधिष्ठिरः ।\nपुनश्च तुमुलं शब्दं श्रुत्वार्जुनमभाषत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing that Dhritarashtra's sons had already fled, and hearing the tumult rise again, Yudhishthira spoke to Arjuna."}},{"n":10,"text":"आचार्ये निहते द्रोणे धृष्टद्युम्नेन संयुगे ।\nनिहते वज्रहस्तेन यथा वृत्रे महासुरे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said: When the teacher Drona was slain in battle by Dhrishtadyumna, as the great asura Vritra was slain by the thunderbolt-bearer,"}},{"n":11,"text":"नाशंसन्त जयं युद्धे दीनात्मानो धनंजय ।\nआत्मत्राणे मतिं कृत्वा प्राद्रवन्कुरवो यथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"the Kurus, downcast, did not hope for victory, Dhananjaya, and fled, thinking only of saving themselves."}},{"n":12,"text":"केचिद्भ्रान्तै रथैस्तूर्णं निहतपार्ष्णियन्तृभिः ।\nविपताकध्वजच्छत्रैः पार्थिवाः शीर्णकूबरैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Some kings fled swiftly in wandering chariots whose rear charioteers were killed, with banners, standards and umbrellas lost and their chariot poles shattered."}},{"n":13,"text":"भग्ननीडैराकुलाश्वैरारुह्यान्ये विचेतसः ।\nभीताः पादैर्हयान्केचित्त्वरयन्तः स्वयं रथैः ।\nयुगचक्राक्षभग्नैश्च द्रुताः केचिद्भयातुराः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Others, confused, mounted chariots with broken seats and frightened horses; some in fear urged on their horses with their feet; others fled in terror in chariots with yokes, wheels and axles broken."}},{"n":14,"text":"गजस्कन्धेषु संस्यूता नाराचैश्चलितासनाः ।\nशरार्तैर्विद्रुतैर्नागैर्हृताः केचिद्दिशो दश ॥","meaning":{"en":"Some were pierced by iron arrows on elephants' shoulders and thrown from their seats, and some were carried off in all ten directions by elephants maddened and fleeing from arrows."}},{"n":15,"text":"विशस्त्रकवचाश्चान्ये वाहनेभ्यः क्षितिं गताः ।\nसंछिन्ना नेमिषु गता मृदिताश्च हयद्विपैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Others, with weapons and armour gone, had fallen from their mounts to the ground, caught in wheel-rims and trampled by horses and elephants."}},{"n":16,"text":"क्रोशन्तस्तात पुत्रेति पलायन्तोऽपरे भयात् ।\nनाभिजानन्ति चान्योन्यं कश्मलाभिहतौजसः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Others fled in fear crying, \"Father! Son!\", and in their dazed confusion they did not recognise one another."}},{"n":17,"text":"पुत्रान्पितॄन्सखीन्भ्रातॄन्समारोप्य दृढक्षतान् ।\nजलेन क्लेदयन्त्यन्ये विमुच्य कवचान्यपि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Others laid their sons, fathers, friends and brothers, who were badly wounded, down, removed their armour, and sprinkled them with water."}},{"n":18,"text":"अवस्थां तादृशीं प्राप्य हते द्रोणे द्रुतं बलम् ।\nपुनरावर्तितं केन यदि जानासि शंस मे ॥","meaning":{"en":"When Drona was killed and the army fled in such a state, who has turned it back? Tell me if you know."}},{"n":19,"text":"हयानां हेषतां शब्दः कुञ्जराणां च बृंहताम् ।\nरथनेमिस्वनश्चात्र विमिश्रः श्रूयते महान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"A great mingled din is heard of neighing horses, trumpeting elephants and rattling wheel-rims."}},{"n":20,"text":"एते शब्दा भृशं तीव्राः प्रवृत्ताः कुरुसागरे ।\nमुहुर्मुहुरुदीर्यन्तः कम्पयन्ति हि मामकान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"These very sharp sounds have risen in the Kuru ocean, and again and again they shake my own men."}},{"n":21,"text":"य एष तुमुलः शब्दः श्रूयते लोमहर्षणः ।\nसेन्द्रानप्येष लोकांस्त्रीन्भञ्ज्यादिति मतिर्मम ॥","meaning":{"en":"This tumultuous, hair-raising noise seems to me as if it could shatter even the three worlds with Indra."}},{"n":22,"text":"मन्ये वज्रधरस्यैष निनादो भैरवस्वनः ।\nद्रोणे हते कौरवार्थं व्यक्तमभ्येति वासवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"I think this is the fearful roar of the thunderbolt-bearer; surely Vasava is coming on the Kauravas' behalf now that Drona is dead."}},{"n":23,"text":"प्रहृष्टलोमकूपाः स्म संविग्नरथकुञ्जराः ।\nधनंजय गुरुं श्रुत्वा तत्र नादं सुभीषणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Our hair stands on end and our chariots and elephants are agitated, Dhananjaya, now that we have heard that dreadful shout of the teacher's son."}},{"n":24,"text":"क एष कौरवान्दीर्णानवस्थाप्य महारथः ।\nनिवर्तयति युद्धार्थं मृधे देवेश्वरो यथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Who is this great chariot-warrior who has rallied the scattered Kauravas and turns them back to battle, like the lord of the gods?"}},{"text":"अर्जुन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Arjuna said:"}},{"n":25,"text":"उद्यम्यात्मानमुग्राय कर्मणे धैर्यमास्थिताः ।\nधमन्ति कौरवाः शङ्खान्यस्य वीर्यमुपाश्रिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Rousing themselves to a terrible deed and taking courage, the Kauravas blow their conches, relying on the strength of him whom I shall name."}},{"n":26,"text":"यत्र ते संशयो राजन्न्यस्तशस्त्रे गुरौ हते ।\nधार्तराष्ट्रानवस्थाप्य क एष नदतीति ह ॥","meaning":{"en":"O king, you doubt who it is that roars after rallying Dhritarashtra's sons now that the teacher, who had laid down his weapons, is dead."}},{"n":27,"text":"ह्रीमन्तं तं महाबाहुं मत्तद्विरदगामिनम् ।\nव्याख्यास्याम्युग्रकर्माणं कुरूणामभयंकरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"I will tell you of that modest, long-armed man who walks like a rutting elephant, whose deeds are fierce, and who gives the Kurus fearlessness."}},{"n":28,"text":"यस्मिञ्जाते ददौ द्रोणो गवां दशशतं धनम् ।\nब्राह्मणेभ्यो महार्हेभ्यः सोऽश्वत्थामैष गर्जति ॥","meaning":{"en":"At whose birth Drona gave a thousand tens of cows as wealth to worthy brahmins; that Ashvatthaman is roaring."}},{"n":29,"text":"जातमात्रेण वीरेण येनोच्चैःश्रवसा इव ।\nहेषता कम्पिता भूमिर्लोकाश्च सकलास्त्रयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As soon as that hero was born he neighed like Uchchaihshravas, and the earth and all three worlds trembled."}},{"n":30,"text":"तच्छ्रुत्वान्तर्हितं भूतं नाम चास्याकरोत्तदा ।\nअश्वत्थामेति सोऽद्यैष शूरो नदति पाण्डव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing it, an unseen being gave him the name Ashvatthaman; that same brave one now roars, Pandava."}},{"n":31,"text":"योऽद्यानाथ इवाक्रम्य पार्षतेन हतस्तथा ।\nकर्मणा सुनृशंसेन तस्य नाथो व्यवस्थितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He whose protector now stands ready, as if a helpless man had been attacked and killed by the son of Prishata through a most cruel deed,"}},{"n":32,"text":"गुरुं मे यत्र पाञ्चाल्यः केशपक्षे परामृशत् ।\nतन्न जातु क्षमेद्द्रौणिर्जानन्पौरुषमात्मनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Drona's son will never forgive that the Panchala seized my teacher by the hair, knowing his own strength."}},{"n":33,"text":"उपचीर्णो गुरुर्मिथ्या भवता राज्यकारणात् ।\nधर्मज्ञेन सता नाम सोऽधर्मः सुमहान्कृतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"You, who know dharma and are a good man, betrayed the teacher with a lie for the sake of the kingdom; that was a very great wrong."}},{"n":34,"text":"सर्वधर्मोपपन्नोऽयं मम शिष्यश्च पाण्डवः ।\nनायं वक्ष्यति मिथ्येति प्रत्ययं कृतवांस्त्वयि ॥","meaning":{"en":"This Pandava, my pupil, is endowed with every virtue and will not say what is false; so he had trust in you."}},{"n":35,"text":"स सत्यकञ्चुकं नाम प्रविष्टेन ततोऽनृतम् ।\nआचार्य उक्तो भवता हतः कुञ्जर इत्युत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then you, wearing the armour of truth as it were, told the teacher falsely that the elephant was dead."}},{"n":36,"text":"ततः शस्त्रं समुत्सृज्य निर्ममो गतचेतनः ।\nआसीत्स विह्वलो राजन्यथा दृष्टस्त्वया विभुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then he threw down his weapon, bereft of attachment and of consciousness, and was agitated, O king, as you saw, the lord."}},{"n":37,"text":"स तु शोकेन चाविष्टो विमुखः पुत्रवत्सलः ।\nशाश्वतं धर्ममुत्सृज्य गुरुः शिष्येण घातितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Overcome by grief and turned away, in love for his son, the teacher abandoned the eternal dharma and was killed by his pupil."}},{"n":38,"text":"न्यस्तशस्त्रमधर्मेण घातयित्वा गुरुं भवान् ।\nरक्षत्विदानीं सामात्यो यदि शक्नोषि पार्षतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having had the teacher killed unrighteously, when he had laid down his weapons, you should now protect the son of Prishata with his ministers, if you can."}},{"n":39,"text":"ग्रस्तमाचार्यपुत्रेण क्रुद्धेन हतबन्धुना ।\nसर्वे वयं परित्रातुं न शक्ष्यामोऽद्य पार्षतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seized by the teacher's son, who is enraged at the loss of his father, we all together shall not be able to protect Dhrishtadyumna today."}},{"n":40,"text":"सौहार्दं सर्वभूतेषु यः करोत्यतिमात्रशः ।\nसोऽद्य केशग्रहं श्रुत्वा पितुर्धक्ष्यति नो रणे ॥","meaning":{"en":"He who has shown great friendliness toward all creatures, having heard of the seizing of his father's hair, will burn us in battle today."}},{"n":41,"text":"विक्रोशमाने हि मयि भृशमाचार्यगृद्धिनि ।\nअवकीर्य स्वधर्मं हि शिष्येण निहतो गुरुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"While I cried out loudly, eager for my teacher's life, the teacher was killed by his pupil, who cast aside his own duty."}},{"n":42,"text":"यदा गतं वयो भूयः शिष्टमल्पतरं च नः ।\nतस्येदानीं विकारोऽयमधर्मो यत्कृतो महान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Our lives have mostly gone and little remains; this great wrong that was done is now the corruption of that remainder."}},{"n":43,"text":"पितेव नित्यं सौहार्दात्पितेव स हि धर्मतः ।\nसोऽल्पकालस्य राज्यस्य कारणान्निहतो गुरुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He was always like a father out of affection, and like a father by dharma; yet that teacher was killed for the sake of a short-lived kingdom."}},{"n":44,"text":"धृतराष्ट्रेण भीष्माय द्रोणाय च विशां पते ।\nविसृष्टा पृथिवी सर्वा सह पुत्रैश्च तत्परैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"O lord of men, Dhritarashtra gave the whole earth, with his devoted sons, to Bhishma and to Drona."}},{"n":45,"text":"स प्राप्य तादृशीं वृत्तिं सत्कृतः सततं परैः ।\nअवृणीत सदा पुत्रान्मामेवाभ्यधिकं गुरुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having gained such a livelihood and always honoured by others, the teacher always chose me above his own sons."}},{"n":46,"text":"अक्षीयमाणो न्यस्तास्त्रस्त्वद्वाक्येनाहवे हतः ।\nन त्वेनं युध्यमानं वै हन्यादपि शतक्रतुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Unwearied, with his weapons laid down in battle by your word, he was killed; otherwise even Indra could not have slain him as he fought."}},{"n":47,"text":"तस्याचार्यस्य वृद्धस्य द्रोहो नित्योपकारिणः ।\nकृतो ह्यनार्यैरस्माभी राज्यार्थे लघुबुद्धिभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Ignoble and shallow-minded, we did treachery to that old teacher, who ever did us good, for the sake of the kingdom."}},{"n":48,"text":"पुत्रान्भ्रातॄन्पितॄन्दाराञ्जीवितं चैव वासविः ।\nत्यजेत्सर्वं मम प्रेम्णा जानात्येतद्धि मे गुरुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Vasavi's son, out of love for me, would give up sons, brothers, fathers, wives and his own life; the teacher knew this."}},{"n":49,"text":"स मया राज्यकामेन हन्यमानोऽप्युपेक्षितः ।\nतस्मादवाक्शिरा राजन्प्राप्तोऽस्मि नरकं विभो ॥","meaning":{"en":"Yet I, wanting a kingdom, looked on while he was being killed. For that, O king, I have fallen head down to hell, O lord."}},{"n":50,"text":"ब्राह्मणं वृद्धमाचार्यं न्यस्तशस्त्रं यथा मुनिम् ।\nघातयित्वाद्य राज्यार्थे मृतं श्रेयो न जीवितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having killed the aged brahmin teacher, who had laid down his weapons like a sage, for a kingdom, death is better for me than life."}}]}]}